<title>USA: Dun &amp; Bradstreet Q1 EPS $0.22 vs adj $0.18.</title>
<headline>Dun &amp; Bradstreet Q1 EPS $0.22 vs adj $0.18.</headline>
<dateline>MURRAY HILL, N.J. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>THE DUN &amp; BRADSTREET CORPORATION</p>
<p>		   CONSOLIDATED STATEMENT OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>		     THREE MONTH COMPARISON OF RESULTS</p>
<p>			 ($ in Millions except for EPS)</p>
<p>					Three Months Ended March 31,</p>
<p>						  (unaudited)</p>
<p>					1997		  1996</p>
<p>				  As Reported	 As Adjusted</p>
<p>Operating Revenue		$459.0		$430.1</p>
<p>Operating Costs		   378.7		 362.8</p>
<p>Operating Income		   80.3		  67.3</p>
<p>Non-Operating Income/</p>
<p>  (Expense) - Net		 (22.5)		(20.0)</p>
<p>Income Before Provision</p>
<p>  for Taxes			  57.8		  47.3</p>
<p>Provision for Income Taxes     19.8		  16.1</p>
<p>Net Income			  $38.0		 $31.2</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share of</p>
<p>  Common Stock		    $0.22		 $0.18</p>
<p>Average Number of Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding		     171.2		 169.7</p>
<p>(In Millions)</p>
<p>NOTE: The 1996 results are on an &quot;as adjusted&quot; basis, which exclude the one-time transaction costs associated with the reorganization, other non-recurring items and the results of divested businesses, and adjust corporate overhead, interest expense and income taxes to anticipated post- reorganization levels.</p>
<p>Compared with 1996 first quarter &quot;as reported&quot; results, revenue increased by $8.6 million, or two percent from 1996 reported revenue of $450.4 million, which included revenue from operations that were subsequently divested.</p>
<p>Net income declined by $26.2 million, or 41 percent, from 1996 reported net income of $64.2 million, or $0.38 per share. The first quarter 1996 reported results included income, net of taxes, of $42.3 million from operations that were sold, spun off or discontinued.</p>
</text>
